{"type":"message","id":"fc0b8b5d","parentId":"c8a88166","timestamp":"2026-10-17T22:45:58.362Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `parse_date` in `dates/parse.py`, and all 3 tests in `tests/test_parse.py` now pass.\n\nThe function used `strptime` with `\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S\"`, a format that has no slot for the trailing `Z` (UTC), so parsing stopped there. It now uses `datetime.fromisoformat(s)` instead.\n\nThings that behave differently now:\n- **`Z` and offsets:** a timestamp ending in `Z` or an offset like `+02:00` now comes back as a timezone-aware datetime. Timestamps with no zone still come back without one, as before. Code that compares or subtracts the two kinds will raise `TypeError`, so anything mixing them needs to normalise first. `day_key` is fine because it only formats the date.\n- **Wider input:** `fromisoformat` accepts more than the old format did, such as date-only strings and fractional seconds.\n- **Python version:** this needs Python 3.11 or newer, since older versions can't parse `Z`. The repo doesn't declare a minimum version. The local interpreter is 3.13.5."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"vertex-anthropic","model":"claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":373,"cacheRead":26486,"cacheWrite":412,"totalTokens":27273,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0},"cttl":{"ephemeral5m":412}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1792277153997,"responseId":"msg_vrtx_011Cg8cyyjsn9dVVX2WhbyA8","duration":4340.817304,"ttft":4246.107597999999,"contextSnapshot":{"promptTokens":26900,"nonMessageTokens":21589,"compactionEpoch":0}}}
